    "content": "The Artemis II crew consists of four astronauts—Commander Reid Wiseman, Pilot Victor Glover, Mission Specialist Christina Hammock Koch (all NASA), and Mission Specialist Jeremy Hansen (Canadian Space Agency)—set to fly a 10-day mission around the Moon in April 2026, marking the first crewed lunar mission in over 50 years. This video shows the crew leaving to meet their families before the launch:59sArtemis II Crew Bids Farewell to Their Families Ahead of Test ...New York PostYouTube• Apr 1, 2026 59s Artemis II Crew Members: Reid Wiseman (Commander): A US Navy veteran and former Chief of the Astronaut Office, this will be his second spaceflight, following a 2014 stay on the International Space Station (ISS). Victor Glover (Pilot): A US Navy captain and test pilot, Glover piloted the SpaceX Crew-1 mission and will be the first Black person to travel beyond low Earth orbit. Christina Hammock Koch (Mission Specialist): An electrical engineer who set a record for the longest single spaceflight by a woman, she will be the first woman to travel beyond low Earth orbit. Jeremy Hansen (Mission Specialist): A Canadian Space Agency (CSA) astronaut and former fighter pilot, he will be the first non-American to fly on a lunar mission. The crew, selected for their diverse experience, will test the Orion spacecraft's life support systems and fly farther from Earth than any human in history.",
